  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\forall d_1\\, d_2 \\in \\mathbb{N},\\; d_1 \\le d_2 \\implies \\mathrm{minEdges}(d_1) \\le \\mathrm{minEdges}(d_2)",
    "plain": "Is the function minEdges(d), giving the minimum number of edges in a graph of dimension exactly d, monotone (non-decreasing) in d?",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Establishes basic structural property of the dimension-edge tradeoff",
      "Would imply superlinear growth of minEdges for d >= 5",
      "Connected to the complete graph optimality conjecture"
    ]
